cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "IMR Nonspherical Dynamics"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - name: "Inertial Microcavitation Rheometry"
abstract: >-
  Python solver for small-amplitude nonspherical perturbations of an inertial
  microcavitation bubble in a soft viscoelastic material. Given a spherical
  radial history, it evolves the spherical-harmonic amplitudes of the interface
  together with the rotational field each mode drives in the surrounding
  medium. Provides NumPy, Numba and JAX backends, the last supporting exact
  parameter sensitivities by automatic differentiation.
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/InertialMicrocavitationRheometry/IMR_nonspherical_dynamics"
url: "https://github.com/InertialMicrocavitationRheometry/IMR_nonspherical_dynamics"
keywords:
  - Python
  - inertial microcavitation rheometry
  - bubble dynamics
  - nonspherical perturbations
  - viscoelasticity
  - automatic differentiation
